{{Quote|She's run this watering hole for a thousand years. Maz is a bit of an acquired taste, so let me do the talking. And whatever you do, don't stare.''"<br />"''At what?''"<br />"Any'' of it.|Han Solo, Rey, and Finn|<ref name="Episode VII" />}}
'''Takodana Castle''', also known as '''Maz Kanata's castle''', or simply as '''Maz's castle''', was located on the [[planet]] of [[Takodana]] on the shore of [[Nymeve Lake]]. The [[castle]] was owned by the [[pirate]] [[Maz Kanata]] up until thirty [[Standard year|years]] after the [[Battle of Endor]] when it was destroyed by the [[First Order]] during the [[Battle of Takodana]].

==Description==
[[File:Takodana_surface_2.png|thumb|right|250px|Takodana Castle was situated on Nymeve Lake.]]
Situated by [[Nymeve Lake]] on [[Takodana]],<ref name="Life Debt" /> this fortress had a main hall and hosted travelers, [[smuggler]]s, [[:Category:Criminals|criminals]], and beings of all walks of life. It had sensor grids and advanced communications gear. Beneath the main levels, the fortress contained dungeons, storerooms, and catacombs which housed tombs of ancient [[Jedi]]. The castle courtyard contained a massive statue of Maz Kanata, gifted to her by her [[Maz Kanata's husband|former husband]].<ref name="CL2016">[[Star Wars: Complete Locations (2016)|''Star Wars: Complete Locations'']]</ref>

==History==
===Kanata's abode===
Takodana Castle<ref name="Smuggler's Guide">''[[Star Wars: Smuggler's Guide]]''</ref> was once occupied by the Jedi and its catacombs contained tombs of [[Jedi Knight]]s.<ref name="Absolutely Everything">''[[Star Wars: Absolutely Everything You Need to Know, Updated and Expanded]]''</ref> It was rumored to have been a [[Battle of Takodana (Jedi versus Sith)|battleground]] for the Jedi and [[Sith]].<ref name="Helmet Collection 52">{{HelmetCollectionCite|52|Databank A-Z}}</ref>

[[File:HanSoloOldSwindler-SoH.png|thumb|left|250px|Han Solo was known to visit Maz Kanata's castle.]]
Approximately a millennium before the First Order-Resistance conflict, Maz Kanata took ownership of the castle and established it as a safe haven for any who came there. All were welcome at Maz's castle so long as they followed the rules, which required no violence of any sort. As such, the castle saw visitors from all walks of life who could generally co-mingle without fear of attack. Kanata strictly enforced the rules personally with the aid of the ancient [[droid]] "[[ME-8D9|Emmie]]"; those who violated them were forbidden from further visits.<ref name="Life Debt" /> To this end, visitors to the castle were greeted by a sign which read "''All are welcome. (No fighting.)''"<ref name="Women of the Galaxy">''[[Star Wars: Women of the Galaxy]]''</ref>

The mantra "NO FIGHTING" was a core rule of Maz Kanata's fortress, with the warning posted in various [[Galaxy|galactic]] [[language]]s.<ref name="CL2016" /> This meant that even those who were in grave trouble, such as having a [[bounty]] on their head, could find refuge at the castle. Such individuals, however, would only be granted one free night of [[Foodstuff|food]], [[water]], and shelter, after which they would have to pay a heavy fee if they wished to remain. The groundskeeper of the castle was [[HURID-327]].<ref name="faceofevil">{{StoryCite|story=The Face of Evil|book=Tales from a Galaxy Far, Far Away: Aliens: Volume I}}</ref>

===Destruction===
{{Quote|First Order scum. The nerve to show up here. How far in the galaxy do I have to go to get away from them?''"<br />"''I might regret asking this, Cookie, but what did they do to you?''"<br />"''They blew up the last place I worked. Maz Kanata's castle. Shame. Such a shame. That's why I took my show on the road. Lucky for you lot.|Strono Tuggs and [[Izal Garsea]]|<ref name="ACoF">''[[A Crash of Fate]]''</ref>}}
Approximately thirty years after the Empire's defeat at Endor, the musicians of the [[Shag Kava]] Band, [[Sudswater Dillifay Glon]], [[Infrablue Zedbeddy Coggins]], [[Ubert Quaril]], and [[Taybin Ralorsa]], played there. Shortly after, the castle was destroyed when the [[First Order]] [[Battle of Takodana|attacked]] the castle in an attempt to capture the droid [[BB-8]].<ref name="Episode VII" /> The destruction of the castle was considered a shame by its head [[chef]], [[Strono Tuggs]], who took his cooking career on the road after the battle. In the end, he would find himself working at [[Black Spire Outpost]] on the planet [[Batuu]], where he would again crosspaths with First Order forces, much to his anger.<ref name="ACoF" />

