==Behind the scenes==
[[File:Maz_castle_cross_section.jpg|thumb|right|300px|A behind the scenes photo by Annie Leibovitz of a group of characters in the castle.]]
Takodana Castle first appeared in the [[2015]] film [[Star Wars: Episode VII The Force Awakens|''Star Wars'': Episode VII ''The Force Awakens'']]. It was first revealed in an exclusive [[Wikipedia:Vanity Fair|''Vanity Fair'']] [http://www.vanityfair.com/hollywood/2015/05/star-wars-force-awakens-photos article] in [[May]] 2015, which included photos by [[Wikipedia:Annie Leibovitz|Annie Leibovitz]]. The pictures showcased one of the sets used for the castle and a number of [[human]], droid, and [[alien]] characters.<ref name="Vanity Fair">{{WebCite|url=http://www.vanityfair.com/hollywood/2015/05/star-wars-force-awakens-photos|text=Star Wars The Force Awakens's Revealed &#124; Vanity Fair|author=Robinson, Joanna|date=2015-05-04|archivedate=20191210223714}}</ref>

In ''The Force Awakens'', the castle's exterior features numerous flags, including one depicting the logo of the real-world [[501st Legion (fan organization)|501st Legion]].<ref name="501FB">{{Facebook|username=The501stLegion|url=The501stLegion/photos/a.164650034751.117031.17637574751/10153843249514752/?type=3&theater|name=501st Legion|date=20-12-2015|quote=As we lift our restrictions on spoilers, we thought it might be appropriate to express thanks for this "Easter egg" in #TheForceAwakens. A variation of the #501st logo flies proudly on a flag at Maz Kanata's castle on the planet Takodana. Thank you to J. J. Abrams and all of the crew at Lucasfilm and Disney for honoring our contributions to the Star Wars franchise. #StarWars #BadGuysDoingGood|archivefile=File:501st_Easter_egg.png}}</ref> In [[Star Wars: Complete Locations (2016)|''Star Wars: Complete Locations'']], Maz's quarters has the theatrical poster of [[Star Wars: Episode IV A New Hope|''Star Wars'': Episode IV ''A New Hope'']] hung on one of its walls.<ref name="Complete Locations">[[Star Wars: Complete Locations (2016)|''Star Wars: Complete Locations'']]</ref>

When approaching the castle, the ''Millennium Falcon'' flies over [[Wikipedia:Derwentwater|Derwent Water]], in the [[Wikipedia:Lake District|Lake District]] in the northwest of [[Wikipedia:England|England]], [[Wikipedia:United Kingdom|UK]].<ref name="Lake District">{{WebCite|url=http://www.manchestereveningnews.co.uk/news/greater-manchester-news/star-wars-filmed-lake-district-10597811|text=Watch: Fascinating video pinpointing exactly where Star Wars scenes were filmed in the Lake District|date=2015-12-14|work=Manchester Evening News|archivedate=20170714174849}}</ref>

